From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] resolver: define the variant selectors for an unresolved build

nanov2_malloc.c splits its code with OS_VARIANT_NOTRESOLVED (definitions
compiled once: policy globals, statistics) and OS_VARIANT_RESOLVED (the hot
paths compiled per resolved variant). The published resolver_internal.h
defines neither, so nano v2 compiled to nothing. macOS builds one variant
with no resolvers (the resolved targets are iOS, tvOS and watchOS only), and
that build needs both halves, so both are 1.

Rebase-risk: low (two definitions).
---
diff --git a/resolver/resolver_internal.h b/resolver/resolver_internal.h
--- a/resolver/resolver_internal.h
+++ b/resolver/resolver_internal.h
@@ -23,4 +23,12 @@
 
 #define OS_RESOLVED_VARIANT_ADDR(s) (void *)(&s)
 
+// NeoDarwin: one unresolved build carries both halves of resolver-split code.
+#ifndef OS_VARIANT_RESOLVED
+#define OS_VARIANT_RESOLVED 1
+#endif
+#ifndef OS_VARIANT_NOTRESOLVED
+#define OS_VARIANT_NOTRESOLVED 1
+#endif
+
 #endif // __MALLOC_RESOLVER_INTERNAL_H__
